WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:07.590
JACK ROONEY: TV producing
workflows are very complex

00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:08.610
and they're layered.

00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:12.270
And it requires an integration
with backend broadcast systems

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:15.310
that can deliver content
to our digital platform.

00:00:15.310 --> 00:00:17.310
Anvato provides that
integration as well as

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:20.730
provides on-prem coding
software and hardware for both

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:22.470
live and VOD.

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:24.350
With their SAS
platform, it enables

00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:26.670
us to do video
management and video

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:29.640
delivery to multiple endpoints,
including mobile as well

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:32.610
as our web VR content
management systems.

00:00:32.610 --> 00:00:35.160
MARK BECK: Cox Media Group
is an integrated broadcast,

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:38.820
publishing, direct marketing,
and digital media company.

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:42.250
The core of our business
is television, radio,

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:43.410
and newspaper.

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:45.630
So the Anvato platform
really allowed

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:49.710
us to design a simpler
and much more flexible

00:00:49.710 --> 00:00:51.360
video architecture.

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:54.030
And it really helped to
take the friction out

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:57.720
of integrating between
our broadcast publishing

00:00:57.720 --> 00:01:01.440
video plants, our CMS,
and the video platform.

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:03.690
BALA SUNDARAMOORTHY: When
we looked at audience trend,

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:06.570
audience is moving from
traditional broadcast

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:09.720
television watching to
watching videos on the web,

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:11.430
on their desktop, to
watching on laptops,

00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:13.320
to watching on their
mobile devices.

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:16.556
One of our key goals is to
be where our audience is.

00:01:16.556 --> 00:01:18.180
So when we wanted to
try to solve that,

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:19.850
we were looking
for a platform that

00:01:19.850 --> 00:01:21.900
allows us to
seamlessly be available

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:23.370
where our audience is.

00:01:23.370 --> 00:01:25.740
Anvato provides a great
platform and an API

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:28.560
that allows us to have the
same player across of all

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:30.969
of these different
delivery content platforms.

00:01:30.969 --> 00:01:33.510
And when we looked at the kind
of content we want to provide,

00:01:33.510 --> 00:01:35.400
we want to make
both our live video

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:38.130
content and video on
demand be available

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:39.600
on all these platforms.

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:42.430
And that's what we were able to
achieve with Anvato platform.

00:01:42.430 --> 00:01:45.060
JACK ROONEY: Video to TV station
source from multiple points.

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:48.260
You could have end-user
submitted video from the field,

00:01:48.260 --> 00:01:50.430
you have camera
folks and reporters

00:01:50.430 --> 00:01:52.530
that are out in the field
covering news events.

00:01:52.530 --> 00:01:55.020
As well as live coverage that
are coming from the broadcast

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:55.830
systems.

00:01:55.830 --> 00:01:59.340
So all of that is key input
into the Anvato platform

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:02.460
that allows those TV
producers to cut and edit

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:03.880
as they see fit.

00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:06.910
And then provide that content
out to the content management

00:02:06.910 --> 00:02:07.710
systems.

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:09.376
BALA SUNDARAMOORTHY:
What we are looking

00:02:09.376 --> 00:02:11.980
for in our video solution
is full integrated

00:02:11.980 --> 00:02:14.920
end-to-end solution
for video, right?

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:16.890
It was key' for us
that the solution

00:02:16.890 --> 00:02:20.430
have a very tight integration to
a broadcast production system,

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:21.780
like Avid.

00:02:21.780 --> 00:02:25.560
It was important to us that it
has robust input capabilities

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:29.730
and ability to get files
through FTP, MRSS, you name it,

00:02:29.730 --> 00:02:30.605
we needed that.

00:02:30.605 --> 00:02:31.980
On the other end
of the scale, we

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:36.230
needed strong output mechanisms,
rollbase syndication and things

00:02:36.230 --> 00:02:37.160
like.

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:40.170
The SAS platform was a
perfect niche fit for us

00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:41.312
from that standpoint.

00:02:41.312 --> 00:02:43.770
JACK ROONEY: We've rolled the
Anvato platforms to our 10 TV

00:02:43.770 --> 00:02:46.140
stations with great success.

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:52.070
We've also integrated with our
Nielsen measurement platform.

00:02:52.070 --> 00:02:54.540
We are about to bring
on our radio stations

00:02:54.540 --> 00:02:56.080
in the very near future.

00:02:56.080 --> 00:02:59.160
So, if you combine that
with all of the things

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:01.320
that we've done from a
measurement perspective,

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:05.727
both on Nielsen and other
measurement platforms,

00:03:05.727 --> 00:03:07.060
Anvato has been a great partner.

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:09.750
And we've had very
good success to date.

00:03:09.750 --> 00:03:13.100
[MUSIC PLAYING]

